course: dictionary
lesson: 5484
title: Lateness and being late
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Lateness means being late: arriving or happening after the right or expected time. It can also mean the late part of the day or night, as in «because of the lateness of the hour».
explain: Lateness is a noun, a word for a thing. You can't count it, so you say «the lateness», not «two latenesses». It comes from the word late, so if you know late, you can work out lateness.
explain: At school, lateness is recorded in the register and may lead to a warning. In polite letters, people write «Please excuse my lateness», which means sorry for being late.
fact: Lateness means being late, or arriving after the right or expected time.
fact: «Being on time shows respect for other people's time.»
fact: Small lateness adds up: 10 minutes late every school day for about 190 days is 1,900 minutes, more than 31 hours of school missed.
fact: Habits help stop lateness: pack your bag the night before, leave a bit earlier, and arrive a few minutes early.
fact: "Irish time" and "island time" are jokes about being relaxed at casual events; they do not count for school, flights or work.
exercise: «Please excuse my lateness.» What does lateness mean here? | Being very early for a party | *Being late | Being happy with a friend | Being tired after a long day
exercise: Ella's mum sits in the car at 9:50 for a 10:00 meeting. What habit is she using to avoid lateness? | Driving very fast | *Arriving a few minutes early | Leaving at exactly 10:00 | Skipping the meeting
exercise: Being 10 minutes late every school day for about 190 days adds up to how many minutes missed? | 19,000 minutes | *1,900 minutes | 190 minutes | 19 minutes
test: «The lateness of the hour meant the shops were already closed.» What does lateness mean here? | Being late for school | A type of late meal | Being on time for a bus | *The fact that it is late in the day or night
test: Which of these is a joke, not a rule for school or flights? | Recording lateness in the register | Arriving a few minutes early | *"Island time" at a casual party | Packing your bag the night before
exam: In a school letter, the teacher writes «Please excuse the lateness of this reply.» What does lateness mean? | Being very kind to the class | A happy surprise | Being late to the school gate | *Being late, arriving after the expected time
